# T-1017: Result.Ok value unification — two Ok calls produce independent types.
# Uses qualified Result.Ok constructor (T-1086: unqualified Ok not in type scope).
# ok1 and ok2 use different payload types (Int vs String), verifying independent types.
[
  Result: [type [Ok a] [Error String]]
  ok1: [Result.Ok 42]
  ok2: [Result.Ok "hello"]
  result: ok1
]
=== out
Dict({"Result": Dict({"Ok": Variant(Result.Ok, Null), "Error": Variant(Result.Error, Null)}), "ok1": Variant(Result.Ok, Int(42)), "ok2": Variant(Result.Ok, String("hello")), "result": Variant(Result.Ok, Int(42))})
